  "basis": "Named Ava Bridge POI 17598272665331 and destroyed rail record 35184412388137 establish the original crossing independently of the neighboring Yadanabon Bridge. No exact-QID map footprint is claimed. Anchor [95.99202543497086,21.871690856512807], heading -0.7194333043712112: +X southeast toward Inwa/Mandalay, -X northwest toward Sagaing, +Z southwest along the Ayeyawady. The nominal 1128 m structure reference, photo-led 966 m principal truss group and 1209.771 m mapped rail extent are recorded separately; extra apron overlap fits standard terrain. Ten bank width samples retain model support at every LOD. Five meet existing paving within 0.000508m at street/closeup; skyline/district simplify the cross-slope and differ by at most 0.136939m. Remaining samples lie above unpaved ground, with at least 0.075m clearance. These are renderer-fit results, not surveyed geographic or historical bank accuracy.",
